    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Investigate a CIA Scenario\r\n\r\nUse this AI Chat level to help you with your case files investigations, as the attacker, defender, or together.\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Tell AI Chat:  \r\n   - Which case file you are working on  \r\n   - The role you are playing (attacker or defender)  \r\n   - Your question  \r\n\r\n**Try it out!**\r\n\r\n:::details [<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Need help figuring out what to ask AI Chat?**]\r\n\r\n### **If you’re the Attacker**\r\nTry asking:\r\n- “Here’s my scenario. What could someone *see, change, or block* here?”\r\n- “Which CIA pillar does this failure point to, and why?”\r\n- “What weakness in the system made this attack possible?”\r\n\r\n### **If you’re the Defender**\r\nTry asking:\r\n- “Given this attacker’s action, what fix would reduce the harm?”\r\n- “How does this fix protect confidentiality / integrity / availability?”\r\n- “What tradeoff might this fix create for real users?”\r\n\r\n### **If you’re stuck on ‘Why It Matters’**\r\nTry asking:\r\n- “Who gets harmed in this scenario, and how?”\r\n- “What real-world consequences could this failure cause?”\r\n\r\n### **If you’re looking for patterns**\r\nTry asking:\r\n- “What do the confidentiality failures in my cases have in common?”\r\n- “Which types of fixes usually help with integrity or availability?”\r\n\r\n:::\r\n",
